{"name":"Pool Table","hex":"#039578","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pool table","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A table used for playing pool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool_table"}],"entries":[{"title":"Billiard table","blocks":[{"text":"A billiard table or billiards table is a bounded table on which cue sports are played. In the modern era, all billiards tables provide an elevated flat surface usually made of quarried slate, that is covered with cloth, and surrounded by vulcanized rubber cushions. More specific terms are used for specific sports, such as snooker table and pool table, and different-sized billiard balls are used on these table types. An obsolete term is billiard board, used in the 16th and 17th centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/A_carom_table_in_Caf%C3%A9_Z%C3%A9phyr%2C_Paris%2C_France%2C_14_January_2007.jpg/330px-A_carom_table_in_Caf%C3%A9_Z%C3%A9phyr%2C_Paris%2C_France%2C_14_January_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billiard_table"},{"title":"Pool (cue sports)","blocks":[{"text":"Pool is a group of cue sports played on a billiard table. The table has six pockets along the rails, into which balls are shot. Of the many different pool games, the most popular include: eight-ball, blackball, nine-ball, ten-ball, seven-ball, straight pool, one-pocket, and bank pool. Eight-ball is the most frequently played discipline of pool, and it is often thought of as synonymous with \"pool\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Niels_Feijen_NL.JPG/330px-Niels_Feijen_NL.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pool_(cue_sports)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%22Billiard_Table_Manufactory%2C_J._M._Brunswick_%26_Bro.%2C_Proprietors%